From 667ee75c4d3793c3b130d56cf578ee9703ec20a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 01:38:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ggml: ROCmFP4/ROCmFPX weight formats behind
 GGML_ARIFI_ROCMFPX_FORMATS

Adopts six serialized weight formats from ROCmFPX at their originator's ids,
exactly as docs/TYPE-ID-ALLOCATION.md section 8 directs: 100 Q4_0_ROCMFP4,
101 Q4_0_ROCMFP4_FAST, 102 Q6_0_ROCMFPX, 103 Q8_0_ROCMFPX, 104 Q3_0_ROCMFPX,
107 Q2_0_ROCMFPX. No metadata gate and no retag tool are owed: none of these
ids has ever meant anything else, so the criterion in section 4 is not met.

GGML_TYPE_COUNT goes to 256, not 108, so block R (200..255) does not force it
to move again. The sparse 44..255 range is fail-closed by code we already had:
gguf.cpp rejects a tensor whose type has blck_size 0, and that is exactly what
an unimplemented id in the range has. 105 and 106 are deliberately NOT taken -
they are ROCmFPX's runtime-only TURBO3_0/TURBO4_0, and 104's geometry is
byte-identical to 105's, so the weight/runtime split has to stay structural.

The gate is a CMake option, not an env var, and the reason is the lesson the
VNNI slot paid for: vec_dot entries are chosen from type_traits_cpu[] at link
time and would sit outside any runtime toggle. A build-time gate covers them by
construction. Default OFF - the mechanism targets Strix Halo and discrete AMD.

The CPU dispatch surface was walked in full, not assumed. Six of the seven
type-id switch sites in ggml-cpu/ops.cpp have a default: label, which is the
silent class that aborted the g128 port at runtime; those get gated cases. The
seventh (clamp) and ggml.c's ftype map are exhaustive over their enums, so
their labels are unconditional - gating them would cost six -Wswitch warnings
per site in the default OFF build, and their bodies are the reject branch,
which is correct in both arms. repack.cpp needs nothing: every arm there is an
exact type equality, so these types reach the terminal nullptr and can never
enter a wrongly-sized x4 struct. Vulkan needs nothing for correctness: every
type-keyed dispatch in supports_op ends in default: return false, so a ROCmFP
tensor falls back to CPU - which is what the ON-path run below actually did.

The ten carve-out files are byte-identical to their ROCmFPX blobs (verified by
blob hash). Note that ggml/rocmfp4/README.md is ROCmFPX's own experiment log:
every number in it is theirs, measured on their hardware, not ours.

Taken-from: charlie12345/ROCmFPX@3edc3d31e
Source-path: ggml/include/ggml.h ggml/src/ggml.c ggml/src/ggml-quants.c ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ops.cpp ggml/src/CMakeLists.txt ggml/rocmfp4/ ggml/rocmfpx/
Ported-mechanism: ROCmFP4/ROCmFPX serialized weight formats and their CPU quant, dequant, validate and vec_dot paths
Origin: ArifiLabs/rocmfp-weight-formats
Evidence: research/local-inference/trial-evidence/110/
Measured-effect: OFF (default) is a no-op on every existing path - no code outside the new ifdefs changes behaviour, and the only unconditional change is GGML_TYPE_COUNT 44 to 256, which grows the ggml type_traits tables and the twelve bool[COUNT] plus eight pipeline[COUNT] arrays in vk_device_struct by 212 ids (estimated ~320 KB per Vulkan device, NOT measured) and lengthens two device-init loops from 44 to 256 trivial iterations. ON was verified end to end on a native artifact - models/rocmfpx-trial/ornith-9b-mtp-kl-Q4_0_ROCMFP4_COHERENT.gguf (257 tensors at type-id 100) loaded in llama-server per F-085 and completed "The capital of France is" with " Paris." at 3.24 tok/s on -ngl 0. OFF refuses the same file fail-closed: "tensor 'output.weight' of type 100 ((null)) has 4096 elements per row, not a multiple of block size (0)". Both ROCmFPX conformance suites pass on our compiler against the ported sources (test_rocmfpx: fp3/fp6/fp8 mse and imatrix weighting; test_rocmfp2_reference: 32520 checks, fingerprint 78389c1c8a0a57a2). No ON-path performance number is claimed - UNMEASURED.
